Context
  Asked to push a gh token into pass and consume it as GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN,
  explicitly not on disk even gitignored; and to fix enable-local-eval. The GitHub
  MCP server is failing this session with 'Authorization header is badly formatted',
  which is what prompted it.

Deviations
  enable-local-eval was the wrong diagnosis on its own. Setting it did not clear the
  prompt, and the screenshot showed the menu bar still present -- which meant the
  profile was not loading at all. --init-directory was the actual cause. Both are
  fixed; only the second explains the symptom.

Considerations
  The stored token is gh's OAuth token (gho_), not a classic or fine-grained PAT. gh
  can rotate it on re-login, at which point the pass copy goes stale silently. For an
  MCP server a dedicated PAT would be more stable, and its scopes could be narrowed --
  this one carries repo, workflow, gist, read:org, user, admin:public_key and
  write:gpg_key, which is more than an MCP server needs.

  Value moved on stdin into pass insert -m, never as an argument, matching
  sync-secrets.sh. Verified by length and prefix only; the value was never printed.

